          "show": [
            "lock",
            "audio"
          ],
          "flow": [
            "dec>lock",
            "lock>audio"
          ],
          "say": "A filter with no weights cleans it up."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "steps",
      "title": "The distillation recipe",
      "say": "Four stations.",
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Teacher reads 12,000 sentences",
          "sub": "saves every value",
          "say": "The teacher reads twelve thousand sentences and saves everything it computed."
        },
        {
          "text": "Small text side copies predictions",
          "sub": "plain L1 losses",
          "say": "A small text side learns to predict those values."
        },
        {
          "text": "Small decoder copies the audio",
          "sub": "spectral, then adversarial",
          "say": "A small decoder learns to turn them into the teacher's audio."
        },
        {
          "text": "Join the halves, store int8",
          "sub": "no joint training",
          "say": "Then the halves are plugged together and stored as eight-bit integers."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "src": "/articles/paradee-tiny-tts/fig2.png",
      "credit": "Paradee paper, Figure 2",
      "title": "Where Kokoro spends its arithmetic",
      "steps": [
        {
          "say": "Where does Kokoro spend its effort?"
        },
        {
          "focus": [
            70,
            8,
            26,
            80
          ],
          "note": "Generator: 89% of the FLOPs",
          "say": "The waveform generator is a quarter of the weights but almost all the arithmetic. Shrinking it buys the speed."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "compare",
      "title": "Getting rid of the buzz",
      "left": {
        "title": "Train it away",
        "items": [
          "Wider critics and phase losses",
          "Larger decoders",
          "The buzz stayed audible"
        ],
        "say": "The small decoder buzzed. Bigger critics and bigger decoders did not fix it."
      },
      "right": {
        "title": "Lock the phase afterwards",
        "items": [
          "Only between 2 and 8 kHz",
          "Follow the helper tone's phase",
          "No parameters, 5% of run time"
        ],
        "say": "So the fix runs afterwards: between two and eight kilohertz, the phase is pulled toward the helper tone."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "src": "/articles/paradee-tiny-tts/fig4.jpg",
