          "say": "The teacher stays detailed above the helper tone."
        },
        {
          "focus": [
            50,
            0,
            50,
            50
          ],
          "say": "The first small decoder blurs there, where it must invent harmonics alone."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "value": "17.8x real time",
      "label": "the released file on one thread of an Apple M4 Pro, phonemes excluded",
      "stamp": "reported",
      "say": "The released file runs about eighteen times faster than real time on one laptop thread."
    },
    {
      "type": "takeaway",
      "text": "Copy the teacher's interface, not its score, and when a small vocoder buzzes, check the band just above its excitation.",
      "mark": "just above its excitation",
      "say": "Copy what the teacher computes, not how it sounds. And check the band just above the helper tone."
    },
    {
      "type": "end",
      "recap": [
        "Each half copies the teacher's saved values",
        "The generator is where the compute lives",
        "A weightless phase lock removes most of the buzz"
      ],
      "say": "To recap: copy each half, shrink the generator, and lock the phase."
    }
  ]
